`runnerRender()` is called on boot (line 800), after scans and after actions — NOT on a periodic poll (the poll is `handoffPoll` every 12 s, which calls `handoffRender()` only, which updates the status line/inputs, not the whole card). Good: a `<details>` won't be re-collapsed by polling.

But careful: `handoffRender()` sets `ho-auto`/`ho-age` values on existing elements — fine inside details.

Also `toolsRender()` (line 800 area) calls `runnerRender()` on every tools re-render (which happens when tools list refreshes — maybe every 30 s?). Let me check if `toolsRender` is called periodically... If yes, an open `<details>` would collapse. Let me grep for a tools poll interval.

To be safe, I'll preserve the open state with a module-level flag captured via `ontoggle`. Simple approach:
```js
let MORE_OPEN = false;
// in markup: <details class="more" id="runner-more" ontoggle="MORE_OPEN=this.open">
...
// after innerHTML: if (MORE_OPEN) document.getElementById('runner-more').open = true;
```
But `MORE_OPEN` must be declared in each app file (mobile, desktop, dashboard). Fine.

