Dashboard has no `ho-more` (no relay card) — but the RESTORE code references `HO_MORE`... no wait, for the dashboard I used the simpler restore without HO_MORE. Good (grep shows 0 ho-more).

Hmm, but dashboard's runnerRender doesn't call handoffRender, and the `ho-more` restore isn't there. Correct.

Now CSS for `.more` in `npm-hub/public/hub.css`. Add after the runner card styles.

Design: a full-width summary line, muted, with a caret. Inside `.runner-btns` (flex), a `<details>` element as a flex item — needs `flex: 0 0 auto` and it will contain a nested `.runner-btns`. Let me make `.more` display:block with width:100% so the nested row wraps below cleanly. In a flex container, a block child with `width:100%` wraps to its own line — that's what I want (the summary on its own line under the buttons).

CSS:
```css
details.more{flex:1 0 100%;margin:0}
details.more>summary{font-size:12px;color:var(--t3);cursor:pointer;padding:6px 0;list-style:none;user-select:none}
details.more>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
details.more>summary::before{content:'⚙ '}
details.more[open]>summary{color:var(--t2)}
```
Using the real gear char in CSS is fine.

Let me add it to hub.css near the runner card block (line ~60).

